{
  "year": 2008,
  "pointsSystem": "2008 used cumulative-TIME scoring (lowest total elapsed time across all four events wins), not a points table - the format that gave the documentary its name 'Every Second Counts'. To fit the shared schema, each event's `points` is that athlete's event time expressed in whole seconds (from the official c3po leaderboard archive), and `totalPoints` is the athlete's cumulative time in seconds across all four events. LOWER IS BETTER. Event points sum exactly to totalPoints, and totalPoints in seconds equals the official overall finish time (e.g. Khalipa 236+157+238+166 = 797 s = 13:17; Matter 418+233+289+210 = 1150 s = 19:10).",
  "sources": [
    "https://c3po.crossfit.com/api/leaderboards/v2/competitions/games/2008/leaderboards?division=1 (official leaderboard archive, men - per-athlete per-event time/seconds; scoreDisplay e.g. '3:56.0' = 236 s)",
    "https://c3po.crossfit.com/api/leaderboards/v2/competitions/games/2008/leaderboards?division=2 (official leaderboard archive, women)",
    "https://games.crossfit.com/workouts/games/2008 (workout cards)",
    "https://web.archive.org/web/20080920204637/http://games.crossfit.com/documents/CFGames08_Top5.pdf (official 'Top 5 in each event' PDF - used to correct the women's Hill Run places, which the c3po API deflates)",
    "https://web.archive.org/web/20080820042821/http://games.crossfit.com/documents/MensCorrectedResults715.pdf",
    "https://web.archive.org/web/20080820035520/http://games.crossfit.com/documents/WomensCorrectedResults715.pdf",
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2008_CrossFit_Games"
